WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.089
Better reflection starts with better questions.

2
00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:04.046
What happened?

3
00:00:04.046 --> 00:00:06.032
What was I trying to accomplish?

4
00:00:06.032 --> 00:00:07.135
What did I expect?

5
00:00:07.135 --> 00:00:08.312
What surprised me?

6
00:00:08.312 --> 00:00:09.783
What evidence do I have?

7
00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:14.123
These questions slow the move from emotional reaction to conclusion.

8
00:00:14.123 --> 00:00:19.640
They help separate the event itself from the first story the mind creates about the event.

9
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.508
Assumption questions are especially useful.

10
00:00:22.508 --> 00:00:28.246
What did I assume about the task, the user, the system, the timeline, the team, or my own skill?

11
00:00:28.246 --> 00:00:32.659
Which assumptions were supported by evidence, and which were guesses?

12
00:00:32.659 --> 00:00:35.528
Many failures are not caused by lack of effort.

13
00:00:35.528 --> 00:00:40.971
They are caused by reasonable-looking assumptions that were never tested soon enough.

14
00:00:40.971 --> 00:00:44.428
Outcome questions connect reflection to improvement.

15
00:00:44.428 --> 00:00:45.311
What worked?

16
00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.194
What failed?

17
00:00:46.194 --> 00:00:47.150
What was lucky?

18
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.474
What was repeatable?

19
00:00:48.474 --> 00:00:50.828
What would I do differently next time?

20
00:00:50.828 --> 00:00:55.020
What should become a checklist, pattern, default, or warning sign?

21
00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:02.523
These questions turn reflection into a practical diagnosis rather than a general feeling that something was good or bad.

22
00:01:02.523 --> 00:01:05.686
Blame questions usually produce weaker learning.

23
00:01:05.686 --> 00:01:06.642
Who is at fault?

24
00:01:06.642 --> 00:01:07.966
Why did I mess this up?

25
00:01:07.966 --> 00:01:09.732
Why did they not know better?

26
00:01:09.732 --> 00:01:13.924
These questions narrow attention and often make people defensive.

27
00:01:13.924 --> 00:01:18.044
Useful reflective questions stay specific and action-oriented.

28
00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:24.664
They ask what the situation teaches, what can be improved, and how the next attempt can be better supported.

29
00:01:24.664 --> 00:01:32.976
The tone matters because people are more likely to learn when the question gives them room to be accurate instead of merely protective.
